	'p_about_cta' => 'Book a first visit →',
	'p_about_h1' => 'About Hisui Clinic',
	'p_about_intro' => 'Founded in 2011 by endocrinologist Helena Varga, Hisui Clinic provides adult endocrinology and diabetes care centered on long-term relationships. We support individuals from age sixteen with clear medical plans followed by the same clinical team over years.',
	'p_about_ix1' => 'Since 2011',
	'p_about_ix2' => 'How we work',
	'p_about_ix3' => 'The building',
	'p_about_s1_b' => 'In 2011, endocrinologist Helena Varga opened Hisui Clinic on Alder Quay to address an ongoing frustration shared by adults living with long-term metabolic and endocrine conditions. In standard healthcare settings, patients often encounter different clinicians at every visit, leaving them with fragmented advice and isolated laboratory readings. Helena established our clinic on an unhurried model where patient care remains consistent across years. We work with adults from age sixteen who require ongoing medical attention for diabetes, thyroid irregularities, and hormone shifts. By keeping clinical oversight with the same physician, we ensure that every therapeutic decision builds thoughtfully upon your documented history rather than starting anew.',
	'p_about_s1_h' => 'Founded in 2011',
	'p_about_s2_b' => 'A chronic endocrine condition demands steady continuity rather than episodic reactions. When you join Hisui Clinic, your primary endocrinologist reviews your lab markers, listens to your daily experiences, and designs a clear medical regimen tailored to your lifestyle. We do not rotate your care among changing practitioners or offer vague suggestions without documentation. Every management strategy is distilled into an agreed written plan that both you and your doctor sign. This structure provides absolute clarity regarding your medication doses, testing intervals, and dietary adjustments, allowing you to move forward with a predictable schedule rather than second-guessing your treatment between appointments.',
	'p_about_s2_h' => 'One doctor, one plan',
	'p_about_s3_b' => 'Living with an endocrine condition takes place in daily routines, far beyond the consulting room. For this reason, our medical plans do not leave you unsupported between quarterly reviews. Our diabetes nurse educators run a dedicated between-visits line available Monday through Friday from 09:00 to 17:00, responding to all clinical questions within one working day. Whether you need guidance adjusting medication doses, interpreting sensor patterns, or preparing for travel, your team remains within reach. This regular contact prevents small uncertainties from escalating into health crises and ensures that your care plan adapts safely as your everyday life evolves.',
	'p_about_s3_h' => 'Continuity and between-visits care',
	'p_about_s4_b' => 'Hisui Clinic is located at 3F, 42 Alder Quay, Harwell Green. Our third-floor rooms were designed to offer a bright, tranquil setting with daylight from generous windows, pale birch furniture, and quiet consulting rooms. The clinic is open Monday through Friday from 08:00 to 18:00 and Saturday from 08:30 to 12:30, remaining closed on Sundays and public holidays. For patients requiring fasting blood tests, our dedicated phlebotomy bay operates strictly between 08:00 and 10:00 on weekdays, ensuring morning samples are drawn efficiently before your primary consultation or workday begins.',
	'p_about_s4_h' => 'The building and access',
	'p_contact_a1' => 'You can book your first visit by calling our reception at +00 21 5840 3317 or emailing hello@hisui-clinic.example. Patient coordinator Claire Mbeki will schedule a complimentary 15-minute phone call to understand your condition, identify the appropriate endocrinologist, and reserve your 60-minute consultation slot. If your consultation requires fresh diagnostic labs, Claire will also book your fasting blood draw between 08:00 and 10:00 on the morning of your visit. Our reception is open Monday through Friday from 08:00 to 18:00 and Saturday from 08:30 to 12:30 to assist you with scheduling.',
	'p_contact_a2' => 'Fasting blood tests are conducted exclusively between 08:00 and 10:00, Monday through Friday, in our dedicated phlebotomy bay on the third floor. Drawing blood during this early morning window ensures that metabolic markers such as fasting plasma glucose, insulin levels, and thyroid hormones are measured under standard physiological conditions. Having samples collected early also allows our partner laboratory to process the panels promptly, ensuring results are ready for your doctor to review during your appointment. We advise patients to fast from midnight, drinking only plain water before their morning arrival.',
	'p_contact_a3' => 'The between-visits line is a dedicated support channel managed by diabetes nurse educators Rosa Almeida and Priya Nair. Available Monday through Friday from 09:00 to 17:00, this service allows active patients to phone or message clinical questions, report side effects, or submit glucose sensor traces. Our nurse educators reply to every inquiry within 1 working day, providing dosage adjustments or scheduling advice agreed with your physician. This service is included with every active plan. Please note that this line is not an emergency service; in an emergency call your local emergency number.',
	'p_contact_a4' => 'Our fees are fully transparent: an initial 15-minute call is free, a 60-minute first consultation with lab review is €160, follow-up consultations are €85, and quarterly plan reviews are €110. Diagnostic thyroid ultrasounds cost €95, sensor start sessions cost €70, and dietitian sessions are €65. Laboratory tests are billed by our partner laboratory. Itemised receipts for your insurer. The between-visits line is included with every active plan. Please give 24 hours\' notice to cancel. Claire Mbeki provides detailed invoices after your visit for submission to private health insurance carriers.',
	'p_contact_a5' => 'Hisui Clinic is situated at 3F, 42 Alder Quay, Harwell Green. Our third-floor clinic is fully accessible by lift from the street-level entrance, providing step-free access for all patients. If arriving by public transit, several central Harwell Green bus routes stop within short walking distance along Alder Quay. Nearby municipal parking bays are available along the quay for patients traveling by car. When you arrive at 42 Alder Quay, enter through the main glass doorway and take the lift directly to the third floor, where Claire Mbeki will welcome you at reception.',
	'p_contact_a6' => 'Yes. Continuity of care is the foundational principle of Hisui Clinic. When you begin treatment with us, you are paired with a specific endocrinologist—Helena Varga for diabetes and metabolic conditions, Tomas Okafor for thyroid and pituitary disorders, or Mei Lindgren for life-stage hormone care. Your 40-minute plan reviews every three months and any interim appointments will always be conducted by your assigned doctor. This ongoing partnership ensures that your physician knows your clinical background thoroughly, enabling subtle, consistent adjustments rather than repetitive introductory conversations at every visit.',
	'p_contact_book_h' => 'Book a first visit',
	'p_contact_book_p' => 'Call the patient coordinator on +00 21 5840 3317, or send us a request. The first call is free and takes 15 minutes; we agree a time for the first consultation and the fasting blood tests together.',
