	'p_diabetes_band' => 'Four areas of diabetes care',
	'p_diabetes_cta' => 'See what a visit costs →',
	'p_diabetes_h1' => 'Diabetes Care',
	'p_diabetes_intro' => 'We manage type 1 diabetes, type 2 diabetes, prediabetes, and diabetes in pregnancy through continuous medical oversight. Every patient follows a structured regimen agreed with their endocrinologist and supported by our diabetes nurse educators and dietitian.',
	'p_diabetes_ix1' => 'Type 1',
	'p_diabetes_ix2' => 'Type 2',
	'p_diabetes_ix3' => 'Sensors',
	'p_diabetes_label' => 'Conditions',
	'p_diabetes_s1_b' => 'We care for adults living with type 1 diabetes through individualized insulin adjustment, technology integration, and regular metabolic reviews. Your primary consultations take place with endocrinologist Helena Varga, while diabetes nurse educators Rosa Almeida and Priya Nair provide intensive technical and practical guidance. Regular 40-minute plan reviews, priced at €110, occur every three months to evaluate HbA1c results, daily insulin profiles, and hypo awareness. Between appointments, you can contact our nurse line Monday through Friday for timely dose fine-tuning. We focus on stabilizing glycemic patterns while helping you maintain full confidence in your work, sports, and daily schedules.',
	'p_diabetes_s1_h' => 'Type 1 diabetes',
	'p_diabetes_s2_b' => 'For type 2 diabetes and prediabetes, we combine structured medical regimens with realistic nutritional changes. Endocrinologist Helena Varga collaborates with dietitian Jonas Reiter to assess your metabolic labs, medication tolerance, and daily eating routines. A 45-minute dietitian session, available at €65, helps you rebuild meals around familiar foods without rigid restrictions. During our €110 quarterly plan reviews, we assess HbA1c trajectories, review oral or injectable medications, and simplify regimens whenever possible. Prediabetes care focuses on halting progression through targeted lifestyle adjustments, regular blood chemistry reviews, and steady encouragement from your dedicated clinical team.',
	'p_diabetes_s2_h' => 'Type 2 diabetes and prediabetes',
	'p_diabetes_s3_b' => 'Managing pre-existing or gestational diabetes requires meticulous blood glucose balance to safeguard both maternal and fetal health. At Hisui Clinic, we coordinate closely with your external obstetric team to align endocrine treatment with your pregnancy care. Endocrinologist Helena Varga and nurse educator Rosa Almeida provide frequent, focused consultations to adjust insulin requirements as pregnancy progresses. We monitor fasting and postprandial glucose levels carefully, reviewing data weekly when necessary. This collaborative framework ensures rapid adjustments to fluctuating hormonal resistance, giving expectant mothers steady guidance and prompt communication through our weekday between-visits line.',
	'p_diabetes_s3_h' => 'Diabetes in pregnancy',
	'p_diabetes_s4_b' => 'Modern sensor technology transforms daily diabetes management by revealing glucose trends in real time. Nurse educator Priya Nair conducts comprehensive 45-minute sensor start sessions for €70, handling physical application, alarm configuration, and software pairing. She teaches you how to interpret trend arrows and review weekly sensor traces accurately. For pump users, we assist with basal rate evaluations and bolus calculation checks. When questions arise regarding skin tolerance or night-shift readings, patients submit traces directly to our between-visits line for review within one working day, ensuring your hardware supports your life smoothly.',
