	'p_fees_h1' => 'Consultation and Service Fees',
	'p_fees_intro' => 'We maintain a clear, transparent fee structure for all consultations, diagnostic procedures, and education sessions. Every active medical plan includes our between-visits nurse line to ensure continuous support throughout your treatment.',
	'p_fees_ix1' => 'Consultations',
	'p_fees_ix2' => 'Tests',
	'p_fees_ix3' => 'Insurance',
	'p_fees_label' => 'Fees',
	'p_fees_s1_b' => 'Our consultation schedule is designed to give you ample time with your specialist without hidden costs. Your initial 15-minute call with patient coordinator Claire Mbeki is entirely free. A comprehensive 60-minute first consultation with lab review costs €160. Routine follow-up consultations of 30 minutes are priced at €85. For patients enrolled in ongoing care, our 40-minute plan review conducted every three months with HbA1c or thyroid labs is €110. Every consultation takes place in private, unhurried surroundings with your designated physician, providing clear explanations and collaborative decision-making at every stage.',
	'p_fees_s1_h' => 'Consultations and reviews',
	'p_fees_s2_b' => 'In addition to medical consultations, we offer on-site diagnostics and specialized education sessions to support your daily care. A 20-minute thyroid ultrasound performed by endocrinologist Tomas Okafor costs €95. For diabetes technology, our 45-minute sensor start session with nurse educator Priya Nair costs €70, covering device fitting, phone pairing, and data interpretation. Personalized nutritional guidance with dietitian Jonas Reiter is available during 45-minute dietitian sessions for €65. All sessions provide practical, actionable tools designed to help you manage your health independently and with total confidence.',
	'p_fees_s2_h' => 'Diagnostic and education services',
	'p_fees_s3_b' => 'Laboratory tests are billed by our partner laboratory. Itemised receipts for your insurer. The between-visits line is included with every active plan. Please give 24 hours\' notice to cancel. Following each appointment, Claire Mbeki provides detailed statements showing standard diagnostic codes for private insurance reimbursement. Because coverage varies between providers, we advise patients to verify their specific outpatient benefits directly with their insurer. If you need to reschedule or cancel an appointment, please notify us at least 24 hours in advance so that we may offer the consulting slot to another patient.',
	'p_fees_s3_h' => 'Laboratory tests, insurance, and booking policy',
