	'p_hormones_band' => 'Four areas of hormone care',
	'p_hormones_cta' => 'Book a first visit →',
	'p_hormones_h1' => 'Hormones Across Life',
	'p_hormones_intro' => 'Led by endocrinologist Mei Lindgren, this clinic addresses hormonal health through adult transitions, including polycystic ovary syndrome, menopause, and bone density preservation. We establish individualized, sustainable medical plans tailored to your long-term vitality.',
	'p_hormones_ix1' => 'PCOS',
	'p_hormones_ix2' => 'Menopause',
	'p_hormones_ix3' => 'Bone density',
	'p_hormones_label' => 'Conditions',
	'p_hormones_s1_b' => 'Polycystic ovary syndrome affects metabolic balance, menstrual regularity, and hormonal patterns across reproductive years. Endocrinologist Mei Lindgren conducts thorough evaluations examining androgen levels, insulin resistance, and cycle history during a 60-minute initial consultation for €160. Rather than offering temporary fixes, Mei develops a multi-faceted medical plan tailored to your symptoms and personal goals. She collaborates with dietitian Jonas Reiter to address insulin sensitivity through enjoyable, everyday meals. Regular reviews allow us to fine-tune therapies, evaluate metabolic markers, and support dermatological or reproductive priorities with steady, compassionate care.',
	'p_hormones_s1_h' => 'Polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS)',
	'p_hormones_s2_b' => 'The menopausal transition involves pronounced shifts in estrogen and progesterone that can cause vasomotor symptoms, mood changes, sleep disturbances, and altered lipid profiles. In our dedicated consultations, Mei Lindgren discusses the safety, benefits, and administration of hormone therapy based on your individual cardiovascular and metabolic risk factors. We review your symptoms systematically, discuss non-hormonal and hormonal options, and establish an agreed regimen documented within seven days. Follow-up appointments at €85 ensure your dosage remains optimal, adjusting therapy as your transition progresses to maintain comfort and long-term cardiovascular health.',
	'p_hormones_s2_h' => 'Menopause care and hormone health',
	'p_hormones_s3_b' => 'Sustaining skeletal strength is a critical element of healthy aging, particularly following menopause or prolonged endocrine imbalances. Mei Lindgren provides focused consultations to review bone mineral density findings and calculate individual fracture risk. When screening is indicated, we issue direct referrals for dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry bone scans with our affiliated diagnostic partners. Following your scan, Mei reviews the density results at her desk, outlining an active management plan that integrates targeted resistance exercise, adequate vitamin D intake, and medical therapies when necessary, scheduling repeat scans typically every two years.',
	'p_hormones_s3_h' => 'Bone density and osteoporosis follow-up',
	'p_hormones_s4_b' => 'Complex endocrine presentations often involve subtle interactions between adrenal hormones and systemic wellbeing. Mei Lindgren conducts thorough assessments for adrenal fatigue investigations, subclinical steroid imbalances, and stress axis irregularities using accurate morning blood tests. When a condition intersects with other medical fields, such as gynecological surgery or specialized imaging, we coordinate referrals directly with trusted hospital specialists. We provide referring clinicians and external teams with comprehensive documentation of your endocrine regimen, ensuring that all aspects of your medical care remain transparent, coordinated, and thoroughly aligned with your primary plan.',
	'p_hormones_s4_h' => 'Adrenal conditions and specialist referrals',
	'p_hormones_tab1' => 'PCOS',
	'p_hormones_tab2' => 'Menopause',
	'p_hormones_tab3' => 'Bone density',
	'p_hormones_tab4' => 'Adrenal and referral',
	'p_news_intro' => 'Keep up to date with notices, scheduling announcements, and clinical guidance from Hisui Clinic in Harwell Green. Our updates are tagged for patients and referring clinicians to provide immediate clarity.',
	'p_news_s1_b' => 'We maintain an active bulletin of operational notices to help patients plan their appointments smoothly. Our standard clinic hours are Monday through Friday from 08:00 to 18:00 and Saturday from 08:30 to 12:30, with fasting blood draws conducted weekdays from 08:00 to 10:00. Any upcoming holiday closures, adjustments to Saturday clinic schedules, or changes to our phlebotomy service are posted here well in advance. We encourage patients to review our latest announcements before traveling to 42 Alder Quay, ensuring your visit proceeds with minimal delay and complete convenience.',
	'p_news_s1_h' => 'Clinic notices and opening hours',
	'p_news_s2_b' => 'Our published articles provide practical recommendations for both active patients and external medical teams. For patients, our clinicians share straightforward instructions on what documentation and medication logs to bring to a first consultation, how continuous glucose sensors fit into daily routines, and how to utilize our weekday between-visits line. For referring general practitioners and specialists, we outline our diagnostic criteria, referral protocols, and laboratory coordination procedures. Each entry features an audience tag so you can quickly identify the clinical or administrative information most relevant to your needs.',
	'p_news_s2_h' => 'Guidance for patients and referring clinicians',
	'p_newsletter_h1' => 'Clinic Newsletter',
	'p_newsletter_intro' => 'Subscribe to receive our monthly clinic bulletin covering schedule updates, Saturday consulting dates, and practical endocrine care insights. We send one concise email per month directly from our Harwell Green clinical team.',
	'p_newsletter_s1_b' => 'Our monthly bulletin keeps patients and referring clinicians informed about operational schedules and educational sessions at Hisui Clinic. We share practical clinic updates, including changes to our weekday hours, upcoming Saturday morning consulting dates, and availability for 45-minute sensor start sessions. In addition, our endocrinologists and nurse educators write brief notes highlighting clinical topics such as preparing for fasting blood tests during the 08:00 to 10:00 window, seasonal schedule reminders, and appointment booking timelines. Each bulletin is prepared directly by our staff to ensure clear, relevant communication without unnecessary promotional clutter.',
	'p_newsletter_s1_h' => 'Monthly updates and clinic announcements',
	'p_newsletter_s2_b' => 'We respect your inbox and handle your contact information with complete confidentiality. When you subscribe, you receive one short note a month about hours and sessions. Unsubscribe any time using the direct link at the base of every message. We never distribute your email address to external third parties or use your contact details for unsolicited marketing. If you ever have questions regarding our clinic policies or wish to adjust your communication preferences, you can reach our patient coordinator Claire Mbeki directly at hello@hisui-clinic.example or by phone at +00 21 5840 3317.',
	'p_newsletter_s2_h' => 'Subscription details and privacy commitment',
	'p_stories_cta' => 'Book a first visit →',
	'p_stories_h1' => 'Patient Stories',
	'p_stories_intro' => 'Long-term endocrine care is shaped by personal routines, working lives, and steady clinical adjustments. Here, four patients share how structured plans and consistent practitioner relationships fit into their everyday lives.',
	'p_stories_ix1' => 'Diabetes',
	'p_stories_ix2' => 'Thyroid',
	'p_stories_ix3' => 'Hormones',
	'p_stories_s1_b' => 'Marta had been managing type 2 diabetes for over six years before contacting Hisui Clinic, feeling exhausted by conflicting nutritional guidelines and frequent clinician turnover. In her case, building stability required aligning medical appointments with her busy working schedule and preserving the foods she enjoyed. Marta moved her regular 40-minute plan reviews to our Saturday morning clinic, allowing her to attend without missing work. During her consultations with dietitian Jonas Reiter, they examined her morning meals and rebuilt breakfasts around what she already cooks at home, avoiding artificial meal replacements. Working together with endocrinologist Helena Varga, Marta\'s medical regimen was reviewed alongside her morning fasting labs and carefully simplified to one tablet change. This focused adjustment, paired with steady Saturday reviews every three months, gave Marta a clear, manageable routine that fits naturally into her everyday life.',
	'p_stories_s1_h' => 'Marta, 58 — Type 2 diabetes',
	'p_stories_s2_b' => 'Working rotating hospital shifts had long complicated Daniel\'s daily management of type 1 diabetes, frequently triggering unexpected nighttime blood glucose fluctuations. In his case, adopting continuous glucose monitoring provided the clarity needed to stabilize his insulin timing around irregular work hours. Daniel attended a 45-minute sensor start session with diabetes nurse educator Priya Nair, who fitted the device on his arm, calibrated the software, and demonstrated how to interpret trend arrows during physical activity. Rather than feeling overwhelmed by continuous streams of glucose data, Daniel sends his weekly sensor trace to our dedicated between-visits nurse line before his block of night shifts. Nurse educator Rosa Almeida reviews the readings and responds with practical recommendations for adjusting his basal rates. Having prompt weekday communication with his clinical team gives Daniel the reassurance needed to navigate demanding night shifts safely and confidently.',
	'p_stories_s2_h' => 'Daniel, 31 — Type 1 diabetes and new sensor',
	'p_stories_s3_b' => 'Aiyana discovered a thyroid nodule during a routine medical examination elsewhere, which initially led to stressful recommendations for immediate surgery without comprehensive ultrasound assessment. In her case, seeking a second opinion at Hisui Clinic brought calm, methodical clarity to the situation. Endocrinologist Tomas Okafor performed a thorough 20-minute thyroid ultrasound directly in our consulting room for €95, carefully evaluating the nodule\'s physical dimensions, margin clarity, and vascular flow while explaining the monitor display to Aiyana in real time. Tomas determined that the nodule exhibited benign features that warranted careful clinical monitoring rather than an invasive, rushed intervention. Together, they established a structured follow-up plan with repeat imaging and thyroid blood panels scheduled every six months. Knowing that the same physician monitors her thyroid health over time has allowed Aiyana to leave uncertainty behind and proceed with quiet confidence.',
	'p_stories_s3_h' => 'Aiyana, 44 — Thyroid nodule follow-up',
	'p_stories_s4_b' => 'As Sofia entered postmenopausal life, she noticed ongoing sleep disruptions, hot flushes, and increasing concerns about her family history of osteoporosis. In her case, understanding her personal skeletal health began with an in-depth consultation with endocrinologist Mei Lindgren. Mei arranged an external dual-energy bone density scan and then reviewed the diagnostic results side by side with Sofia at her consulting desk, explaining the T-scores and fracture risk calculations in plain English. Rather than recommending generic supplements, Mei formulated a tailored bone preservation plan that combined structured resistance exercise, optimized dietary vitamin D intake, and tailored hormonal therapy to alleviate her daytime vasomotor symptoms. They scheduled a follow-up bone scan in two years to monitor bone density changes methodically. Sofia now follows a balanced, documented health strategy supported by regular check-ins with her dedicated endocrinologist.',
	'p_stories_s4_h' => 'Sofia, 52 — Menopause and bone density',
	'p_team_f1' => 'All',
	'p_team_f2' => 'Doctors',
