	'p_team_p4_n' => 'Rosa Almeida',
	'p_team_p4_r' => 'Diabetes nurse educator',
	'p_team_p5_l' => 'Sensor start sessions and insulin pump support.',
	'p_team_p5_n' => 'Priya Nair',
	'p_team_p5_r' => 'Diabetes nurse educator',
	'p_team_p6_l' => 'Builds meal plans around what you already cook.',
	'p_team_p6_n' => 'Jonas Reiter',
	'p_team_p6_r' => 'Dietitian',
	'p_team_p7_l' => 'First calls, laboratory slots and itemised receipts.',
	'p_team_p7_n' => 'Claire Mbeki',
	'p_team_p7_r' => 'Patient coordinator',
	'p_team_s1_b' => 'Our team of physicians provides expert clinical direction across complex metabolic and hormonal conditions. Helena Varga is the founder of Hisui Clinic and an endocrinologist focusing on type 2 diabetes, metabolic syndrome, and establishing long-term medical plans. Tomas Okafor is an endocrinologist specializing in thyroid and pituitary disorders, performing on-site thyroid ultrasound evaluations. Mei Lindgren is an endocrinologist concentrating on hormones across life, guiding patients through polycystic ovary syndrome, menopause transitions, and bone density preservation. Each physician sees patients individually, ensuring that your care is directed by the same dedicated doctor throughout your entire treatment.',
	'p_team_s1_h' => 'Endocrinologists',
	'p_team_s2_b' => 'Our diabetes nurse educators provide vital day-to-day support, education, and technical guidance. Rosa Almeida is a diabetes nurse educator who manages our between-visits line, reviewing daily inquiries, addressing medication questions, and ensuring smooth communication between appointments. Priya Nair is a diabetes nurse educator who leads our sensor start sessions, teaching patients how to fit, calibrate, and interpret continuous glucose monitoring sensors and insulin pumps. Together, Rosa and Priya ensure that our patients feel confident handling technical equipment and daily adjustments in their ordinary home and working environments.',
	'p_team_s2_h' => 'Diabetes nurse educators',
	'p_team_s3_b' => 'Lifestyle and operational coordination complete our patient care framework. Jonas Reiter is our clinic dietitian, conducting 45-minute nutrition sessions for €65. Jonas collaborates closely with patients to adapt everyday meals around familiar foods, supporting blood sugar stability without rigid or stressful eating regimes. Claire Mbeki is our patient coordinator, managing your initial 15-minute phone calls, scheduling lab appointments for the 08:00 to 10:00 fasting window, and issuing itemized receipts for insurance reimbursement. Claire ensures that all organizational aspects of your visits run smoothly from your very first contact.',
	'p_team_s3_h' => 'Dietitian and patient coordinator',
	'p_team_side' => 'The seven of us',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_band' => 'Three areas of thyroid and pituitary care',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_h1' => 'Thyroid and Pituitary Care',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_intro' => 'Our clinic provides comprehensive diagnostics and long-term medical management for underactive and overactive thyroid conditions, thyroid nodules, and pituitary disorders. Care is led by endocrinologist Tomas Okafor with on-site ultrasound evaluations.',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_ix1' => 'Thyroid',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_ix2' => 'Nodules',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_ix3' => 'Pituitary',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_label' => 'Conditions',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_s1_b' => 'Endocrinologist Tomas Okafor evaluates and treats autoimmune and systemic thyroid conditions, including Hashimoto thyroiditis and Graves disease. Managing thyroid dysfunction requires balancing hormone levels through precise medication dosing rather than broad assumptions. We conduct detailed initial consultations for €160, accompanied by morning thyroid blood tests between 08:00 and 10:00. Once your treatment begins, follow-up consultations of 30 minutes at €85 or quarterly reviews at €110 track free T4 and TSH levels. We ensure symptoms such as fatigue, weight shifts, temperature intolerance, and palpitations are addressed through methodical adjustments followed over years.',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_s1_h' => 'Underactive and overactive thyroid',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_s2_b' => 'Discovering a thyroid nodule often brings anxiety, but most nodules can be managed safely with systematic observation. Tomas Okafor performs dedicated 20-minute thyroid ultrasound examinations directly in our consulting rooms for €95. Having imaging conducted by your treating endocrinologist allows immediate discussion of nodule dimensions, margins, and vascularity without external delays. Rather than rushing into unnecessary interventions, we establish clear follow-up intervals, typically scheduling repeat scans and clinical examinations every six to twelve months. This calm, methodical surveillance ensures any physical changes are documented accurately while sparing you unneeded distress.',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_s2_h' => 'Thyroid nodules and clinical ultrasound',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_s3_b' => 'Disorders of the pituitary and adrenal glands require careful endocrine monitoring to maintain vital hormone equilibria. Tomas Okafor oversees long-term follow-up for conditions such as pituitary microadenomas, hyperprolactinemia, secondary adrenal insufficiency, and cortisol dysregulation. Because these hormones interact across complex feedback loops, we coordinate specific morning blood panels with our partner laboratory. Follow-up consultations allow us to evaluate hormone replacement therapies, monitor clinical symptoms, and determine appropriate intervals for surveillance imaging. We provide consistent oversight so your pituitary and adrenal management remains stable and thoroughly documented across each stage of life.',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_s3_h' => 'Pituitary and adrenal follow-up',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_tab1' => 'Thyroid',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_tab2' => 'Nodules and ultrasound',
	'p_thyroid-pituitary_tab3' => 'Pituitary and adrenal',
	'p_thyroid_cta' => 'Ultrasound and follow-up fees →',
	'p_your-plan_band' => 'Five parts, one written plan',
	'p_your-plan_h1' => 'Your Care Plan',
	'p_your-plan_inter' => 'Fasting tests 08:00–10:00 open every working morning.',
	'p_your-plan_intro' => 'Every patient at Hisui Clinic follows a transparent, five-part medical pathway designed to deliver continuity, clarity, and unhurried clinical support. We establish a written regimen with the same doctor and provide reliable nurse access between appointments.',
	'p_your-plan_ix1' => 'First call',
	'p_your-plan_ix2' => 'Reviews',
	'p_your-plan_ix3' => 'Between visits',
	'p_your-plan_label' => 'Your plan',
	'p_your-plan_s1_b' => 'Our care pathway is structured into five distinct stages to ensure complete transparency from your very first inquiry. It begins with a complimentary 15-minute phone call with patient coordinator Claire Mbeki to discuss your needs and book appropriate lab slots. Next, you attend a 60-minute comprehensive first consultation with your doctor, following a morning fasting blood draw. Within 7 days, your doctor and you sign an agreed one-page written regimen. Every 3 months, you attend a 40-minute plan review with the same physician. Finally, our between-visits nurse line provides ongoing advice between scheduled appointments.',
	'p_your-plan_s1_h' => 'The five-part pathway',
	'p_your-plan_s2_b' => 'Your 60-minute initial consultation with your endocrinologist costs €160 and provides the time necessary to explore your medical history in depth. Patients arrive between 08:00 and 10:00 for fasting blood tests so that fresh laboratory values are ready for review during the clinical discussion. Following this examination, your doctor formulates a concise, one-page written regimen delivered within 7 days. This document outlines your diagnostic findings, medication schedules, lifestyle targets, and testing timelines. Because both you and your physician sign this plan, everyone remains aligned on the precise clinical direction.',
	'p_your-plan_s2_h' => 'First consultation and agreed regimen',
	'p_your-plan_s3_b' => 'Our clinic operates around four fundamental process standards: 60 minutes for your first consultation, 7 days to deliver your agreed written plan, 3 months between regular review appointments, and 1 working day to reply to between-visits inquiries. Every three months, you return for a 40-minute plan review (€110) with your dedicated endocrinologist. We examine your updated HbA1c or thyroid blood work, assess your response to medications, and refine your plan. By maintaining this consistent three-month cadence with the same doctor, we catch subtle physiological changes early and adjust treatment safely.',
	'p_your-plan_s3_h' => 'Quarterly reviews and process figures',
	'p_your-plan_s4_b' => 'Between scheduled consultations, active patients have direct access to our dedicated between-visits line staffed by diabetes nurse educators Rosa Almeida and Priya Nair. Open Monday through Friday from 09:00 to 17:00, this service allows you to submit questions, report symptoms, or share sensor traces, with a reply within 1 working day. This communication channel is included with every active plan at no extra charge. Please note that this line is not an emergency service. In an emergency call your local emergency number immediately or visit the nearest hospital emergency department.',
	'p_your-plan_s4_h' => 'Between-visits nurse line and emergency guidelines',
